    "title": "Masters leaderboard, cut tracker results today: Rory McIlroy leads, Bryson DeChambeau misses cut",
    "text": "Updated April 10, 2026, 7:30 p.m. ETRory McIlroy leads the 2026 Masters tournament at -12 after the second round.The cut line for the weekend was set at +4, with Bryson DeChambeau among those who missed it.McIlroy is also the current betting favorite to win the tournament at Augusta National.The article also provides a detailed TV and streaming schedule for the weekend rounds.The Masters 2026 second round has come to a close at Augusta National Golf Club Friday, as the live leaderboard has an official cut line, and some favorite golfers are no longer competing in the year's first PGA major.Here's what to know about the Masters leaderboard and cut line, how to watch, odds, and more:Masters 2026 leaderboard updates today, Friday, April 10: Who is leading The Masters golf tournament at Augusta National Golf Club after Round 2?1. Rory McIlroy -12 (F)2T. Sam Burns -6 (F)2T. Patrick Reed -6 (F)4T. Justin Rose -5 (F)4T. Shane Lowry -5 (F)4T. Tommy Fleetwood -5 (F)7T. Wyndham Clark -4 (F)7T. Tyrrell Hatton -4 (F)7T. Haotong Li -4 (F)7T. Kristoffer Reitan -4 (F)7T. Jason Day -4 (F)7T. Cameron Young -4 (F)Visit masters.com or pgatour.com for full leaderboard results.Watch The Masters on SlingMasters 2026 cut line today: Bryson DeChambeau misses The Masters cut. Who else missed the cut?The Masters cut line is +4, according to masters.com. Here are a few top golfers who missed the cut, or were in danger of missing the cut.Jon Rahm +4 (F) − INBryson DeChambeau +6 (F) − MISSED CUTRobert MacIntyre +7 (F) − MISSED CUTMin Woo Lee +11 (F) − MISSED CUT Watch The Masters on PrimeThe Masters 2026 odds: Who is the favorite to win The Masters golf tournament at Augusta National Golf Club?The current favorite is Rory McIlroy after finishing 6 strokes ahead of his nearest competitor by the end of the second round, according BetMGM. Visit BetMGM for the latest odds on The Masters 2026 golf tournament.2026 Masters TV schedule this weekend: What channel is The Masters on TV? How to stream, where to watch Masters golf tournament this week2026 Masters TV schedule tomorrow, Saturday, April 11: where to watch PGA golf tournament\"Mornings at the Masters\": 9-9:45 a.m., Masters YouTubeOn The Range: 10 a.m.-noon ET, Masters.com | CBS Sports Digital | CBS Sports Network | Paramount+ (Apple Store / Google Play Store)Featured Groups: 10:15 a.m.-7 p.m. ET, Masters.com | CBS Sports Digital | ESPN App (Apple Store / Google Play Store) | Paramount+ (Apple Store / Google Play Store) | Prime VideoHoles 4, 5 & 6: 10:30 a.m.-3:30 p.m. ET, Masters.com | ESPN App (Apple Store / Google Play Store)Amen Corner: 11:45 a.m.-6 p.m. ET, Masters.com | CBS Sports Digital | ESPN App (Apple Store / Google Play Store) | Paramount+ (Apple Store / Google Play Store) | Prime VideoInside Amen Corner: 11:45 a.m.-6 p.m., Masters.com | Prime VideoHoles 15 & 16: 11:45 a.m.-7 p.m. ET, Masters.com | CBS Sports Digital | ESPN App (Apple Store / Google Play Store) | Paramount+ (Apple Store / Google Play Store) | Prime VideoThird Round Broadcast: noon-7 p.m. ET, Masters.com | Paramount+ (Apple Store / Google Play Store); 2-7 p.m. ET, CBS | 5-6 p.m. ET, ESPN DeportesRadio Coverage: 2-8 p.m., SiriusXM, Channel 92Watch The Masters on ESPN2026 Masters TV schedule, Sunday, April 12: where to watch PGA golf tournament\"Mornings at the Masters\": 9-9:45 a.m., Masters YouTubeOn The Range: 10 a.m.-noon ET, Masters.com | CBS Sports Digital | CBS Sports Network | Paramount+ (Apple Store / Google Play Store)Featured Groups: 10:15 a.m.-7 p.m. ET, Masters.com | CBS Sports Digital | ESPN App (Apple Store / Google Play Store) | Paramount+ (Apple Store / Google Play Store) | Prime VideoHoles 4, 5 & 6: 10:30 a.m.-3:30 p.m. ET, Masters.com | ESPN App (Apple Store / Google Play Store)Amen Corner: 11:45 a.m.-6 p.m. ET, Masters.com | CBS Sports Digital | ESPN App (Apple Store / Google Play Store) | Paramount+ (Apple Store / Google Play Store) | Prime VideoInside Amen Corner: 11:45 a.m.-6 p.m., Masters.com 